course: dictionary
lesson: 4323
title: Growing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word growing can mean more than one thing, so the words around it tell you which meaning fits. Look at the clues. «Egyptians had three seasons: the flood, the growing time and the harvest.» Here growing time is a season for raising crops, so it means the time when plants are grown.
explain: «A growing child is not a small grown-up.» Here growing means getting bigger over time. Try the swap check: "A getting-bigger child is not a small grown-up" still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Growing can also mean increasing. «A growing number of children read every day» means the number is getting bigger. Always ask: is something getting bigger, or is something being raised? The clues will tell you.
fact: Growing means getting bigger or taller, right now or over time.
fact: Growing plants means raising them from seeds.
fact: Growing can mean increasing or becoming more, as in «a growing number of» people.
fact: «Growing up» means getting older and bigger, and real growing is slow and steady.
fact: The growing season is the warm part of the year, when plants are raised.
exercise: «Egyptians had three seasons: the flood, the growing time and the harvest.» In this sentence, growing time means | *The part of the year when crops are raised | The time after the harvest is finished | A time for sleeping late
exercise: «In cartoons a character shoots up overnight, but real growing is slow, steady and full of surprises.» What is real growing like? | *Slow, steady and full of surprises | Happening in one night | Never happening at all | Fast, like a magic potion
exercise: «A growing number of children read every day.» What does a growing number mean? | *The number is getting bigger | The number is getting smaller | The number is written in words | The number has stopped
test: «Growing plants means raising them from seeds.» Growing plants means | Pulling them up by the roots | Breaking them into pieces | Painting them green | *Raising them from seeds
test: «The growing season is the warm part of the year, and a growing plant needs water and light.» What does a growing plant need? | *Water and light | Snow and ice | Only darkness | Sweets and sugar
exam: Which word can replace growing in «a growing crowd» without changing the meaning? | *increasing | shrinking | sleeping | empty
